  "notes": "どこか is an indefinite word meaning \"somewhere\" or \"somehow.\" Part of the ka-series indefinites.\n\nFUNCTIONS:\n1. Location (somewhere): どこか⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{行|い}く→行く：00119_iku⟧ (go somewhere)\n2. Manner (somehow, somewhat): どこか⟦{変|へん}→変：01124_hen⟧⟦だ→だ：09496_da⟧ (somehow strange)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- どこか⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: to/at somewhere\n- どこか⟦で→で：00502_de⟧: at somewhere (action location)\n- どこか⟦へ→へ：02473_he⟧: toward somewhere\n\nRELATED INDEFINITES:\n- ⟦{何|なに}か→何か：03873_nanika⟧: something\n- ⟦{誰|だれ}か→誰か：02912_dareka⟧: someone\n- ⟦いつか→いつか：01809_itsuka⟧: sometime\n- ⟦どれか→どれか：22606_doreka⟧: one of them\n\nUSAGE:\nWhen modifying an adjective without a particle, どこか means \"somewhat\" or \"in some way\": どこか⟦{寂|さび}しい→寂しい：00880_sabishii⟧ (somehow lonely).",
